---
name: ptt-nudges
description: "Turn nudges (automatic cross-session messages telling a session that its inbox has news) on or off for every session of this project, or show the switch. Arguments: on, off, or none."
disable-model-invocation: true
---

# Nudges on or off

The command, or an AtE naming these records, approves the records this skill
writes (it writes none: the switch is a local setting beside the records);
other work needs AtE (rules file).

- No argument: `<records>/bin/ptt nudges`: report whether nudges are on.
- `on` or `off`: `<records>/bin/ptt nudges on|off`, then report the state.
  The switch is shared by every session of the project.

Off, `ptt` prints no nudge targets, and a session that subscribed before
sends nothing on the idle notice. Nothing is lost: the inbox and the unseen
items in `<records>/bin/ptt who` show every item. Turning nudges on sends
nothing for earlier items.
